<title>FINLAND: Nokia rises after H1 results.</title>
<headline>Nokia rises after H1 results.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Finnish telecoms group Nokia Oy rose on Monday after the group reported higher than expected first-half earnings, brokers said.</p>
<p>At 1620/1320 GMT, Nokia A traded 4.50 markka (81 cents) higher at 477.00 markka.</p>
<p>&quot;The result is excellent, but after the recent rises there is still some selling pressure,&quot; one broker said.</p>
<p>Nokia's H1 profit at 3.33 billion markka clearly beat the 3.09 billion forecast in a Reuters poll and exceeded the highest forecast at 3.30 billion.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom +358 - 0 - 680 50 242, news@reuters.fi ($ = 5.552 Finnish Markka)</p>
